  "context_pill": "Marginal Relief under Section 87A",
  "example_summary": "Computation of tax liability of Mr. Nitin under default tax regime Section 115BAC for A.Y. 2026-27 featuring marginal relief.",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Eligibility / Benchmark | Operative Rule / Threshold | Legal & Tax Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 115BAC** | Individuals, HUFs, AOPs, BOIs, AJPs | Default Tax Regime with concessional slab rates | Tax computed as per statutory slab rates under Section 115BAC. |\n| **Section 87A (Full Rebate)** | Resident Individual under Section 115BAC | Total Income $\\le$ Statutory Threshold | 100% Tax Rebate up to maximum statutory limit (Tax becomes Nil). |\n| **Section 87A (Marginal Relief)** | Resident Individual under Section 115BAC | Total Income slightly exceeds Statutory Threshold | Tax before Cess limited to excess income over the statutory threshold. |\n| **Finance Act (Cess)** | All Assessees | Computed on net tax after rebate | Health and Education Cess @ 4% added to tax liability. |\n\n### Statutory Rule Checklist\n\n* **Section 115BAC Concessional Regime**: Applies by default unless the assessee validly opts out to the normal regime.\n\n* **Marginal Relief Formula under Section 87A**:\n  - Step 1: Calculate Incremental Income $(A) = \\text{Total Income} - \\text{Threshold Income}$\n  - Step 2: Calculate Tax on Total Income $(B)$ under Section 115BAC slab rates\n  - Step 3: If $B > A$, Marginal Rebate u/s 87A $= B - A$\n  - Step 4: Net Tax before Cess $= B - (B - A) = A$\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Mandatory Application of Marginal Relief: Marginal relief under Section 87A ensures that an assessee earning slightly above the rebate threshold is not penalized with a tax liability higher than the extra income earned.",
